    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrĕus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of earth</i>, <i>earthen</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrea progenies duris caput extulit arvis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 2, 341</span></i>
			 (al. ferrea, Rib.): fossa et terreus agger, <i>a
				dam</i> or <i>dike of earth</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 14, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. L. L. 5, § 48</span></i>
			 Müll.</div>
